Hello Beautiful People,

Since May, we have accepted several bug-fixes and enhancements from a
bunch of contributors and are happy to announce a new release.

Magic Wormhole is a Python library and CLI tool to securely get
arbitrary data from one computer to another using short, one- time,
human- pronounceable codes and end-to-end encryption.

The library allows use of the lower-level protocol for things besides
file-transfer.

New features added include:

 - upgrade CI to follow "zizmor" recommendations (@meejah)
 - documentation for "your-address" feature in the Mailbox Server (@meejah)
 - nicer message on "crowded" error (@mvanhorn)
 - ignore incoming "transit" message when doing text-message (@kenny-ish)
 - add "winget" instructions for Windows users (@koppor)
 - link iyox-wormhole in ecosystem (@DodoLeDev)
 - earlier error display for invalid --transit-helper options (@the8thbit)

The following bugs have been fixed:

 - fix where "completion" files are installed (@mvanhorn)
 - TLS for main relay, add wormhole.page to docs (@dongdigua)
 - better permissions on authorized_keys creation (@NiBi8z)
 - documentation typos and links from (@lesteve, @michaelbnewman, @Cycloctane)
 - several CI cleanups (@ikmckenz)
 - export all "Status" API enums / union-types (@wolfgang-aura)
 - honour --code-len for SSH key transfer (@ikmckenz)
 - strip suid bits on Zip file extract (@ikmckenz)


You can find the release on PyPI:

   https://pypi.org/project/magic-wormhole/

More information can be found:

   https://magic-wormhole.readthedocs.io/en/latest/welcome.html
   https://github.com/magic-wormhole/magic-wormhole


thanks,

meejah
